| A pushed particle gets an *answer*: whatever the program's handler
| returned, handed back to the module that pushed it
| (`code_module_inbound_reply`, see code_abi.h).
|
| That is what lets a module ask a question rather than only announce
| something — an HTTP server pushing a `Request` and needing a response is
| the case it was built for. Nothing new is written on this side: a handler
| answers a pushed particle exactly as it answers any other, by returning
| one.
link "native_modules/test_events.so" as ev

Tick { value } => {
    return Ack { value = value + 100 }
}

emit Start { value = 3 } to ev get started
assert started.value = 3

| The three ticks have been handled by here, and each answer went back.
emit Answers {} to ev get a
assert a.count = 3
assert a.last = 102
